==Enemy==
A decently-rounded, high-damaging enemy with [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]]-level range and lots of knockbacks, almost like an enemy counter to the player's [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]]. They have very high damage for their health, with a 1:3 attack power to health ratio.

Teacher Bear has a rather high money drop, making them a good income source in many of the later stages they appears in.

==Strategy==
Teacher Bear is less of a threat than [[Le'boin]] due to their inferior health, shorter range and very high knockback count, making them vulnerable to a large stack of [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cats]] or any other fast attacker like [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]]. They can also be easily defeated by [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], who has enough health to tank their attacks, or by a stack of [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cats]], as they outrange Teacher Bear and deal good damage. However, beware of any peons they support, as their 10 knockbacks can also allow them to reposition themselves due to their range. They aren't a strong enemy and won't push much if you hit them every so often. In fact, many of their [[Ursamajor|colored]] [[Cadaver Bear|variants]] are more threatening than Teacher Bear. Overall, they should be treated like a glass-cannon ranged attacker.

Later in the game, use stacks of ([[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]) Dragon Cats, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], or any [[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|Backliner-class]] and higher-ranged [[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|Midranger-class Cats]] that outrange them as they can easily defeat him. If they are shielded by other enemies in front of them, [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] will also be effective, with examples ranging from [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] to [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]].

