==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = Teacher Bear
|Assassin Bear
|Teacher Bear's [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] variant. He possesses extreme speed, DPS and range yet has less money drop and health, so low that even the [[Cat Cannon]] can take him out when not buffed to an extent. Often used in gimmicky stages as a makeshift time limit, as he mostly guarantees the player's loss if heavily buffed/spammed or if the Cannon isn't prepared.
|Bears Be Bare
|A group of bears sitting together on a bleacher introduced in the [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]] event.
|Bearkini
|A much faster variant of Teacher Bear wearing a bikini. First encountered in the [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] event.
|Mighty Gui Zuli
|A buffer variant of Teacher Bear introduced in the [[Old Guys About Town (Monthly Event)|Old Guys About Town]] event. This enemy has a higher overall DPS with its increased attack rate and damage while having only three knockbacks.
|Ursamajor
|An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Teacher Bear. Possesses superior overall stats and strengthens by 100% at 50% health.
|The Red Malice
|A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Mighty Gui Zuli. Compared to Zuli, The Red Malice is much faster and attacks more often, but has more knockbacks, less damage, less range, and a 100% chance to knockback Cat Units on hit.
|Cadaver Bear
|[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Teacher Bear. Attacks much faster, can burrow under Cat Units and revives once with 100% HP.
|Teacher Cybear
|[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of Teacher Bear. Has single-target attacks with extreme damage, range and attack rate.
|Bears Be Back
|A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Bears Be Bare introduced in the [[Bears Be Back (Monthly Event)|Bears Be Back]] event. Compared to Bears Be Bare, they have the same health, higher range, slower movement speed, a multi-hit attack, and the ability to afflict cats with a wide range of debuffs. They have the most traits out of every enemy in the game.
|MikuBear
|A Teacher Bear variant from the [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event]]. It has higher stats, but is Single Target.
|Fallen Bear
|An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Teacher Bear. His health and range are both subpar for his very high DPS, but he has a durable [[Shield]] and creates a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]] upon death.
|Demon Teacher Bear
|A Teacher Bear variant from the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. Attacks quite rapidly, has a 20% chance to do a Savage Blow for 3x damage and can weaken units to 50%.
|Pinky Bear
|A Teacher Bear variant from the [[PAC-MAN Collaboration Event]]. Has a 50% to Knockback/Slow Cats as well as 4x more health and a faster attack rate.
}}

