==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]], Teacher Bear's description was:
<pre>
A kindergarten teacher. He LOVES children.
His sharp claws are not suited for the job.
Not related to a certain other bear.
No one knows his real name.
</pre>
**The pre-14.7 description referenced [[wikipedia:Pedobear|Pedobear]], who has been frequently misinterpreted as a symbol of pedophilia, despite being purposed to notify people against such acts. It was presumably changed to avoid association with Pedobear.
**Although the pronouns in Teacher Bear's description were changed to they/them, [[Teacher Cybear]]'s description was not updated accordingly, meaning Cybear's still refers to Teacher Bear as he/him.
*[[Teacher Bun Bun]] is Teacher Bear's former master.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]] was convinced to join the Cat Army because Teacher Bear said, "Girls are most cute with a Cat in hand!'"
*According to [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]'s description, Teacher Bear has a popular drama named after them: "Trial of Teacher Bear".
*Teacher Bear and [[The Face]] were the first enemies to have variants, as [[Assassin Bear]] and [[Shy Boy]] have existed since [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]].
*Ironically, Teacher Bear did not appear in [[Kumanchu Royale]], a game all about bears. However, [[Assassin Bear]] was present, and had a new [[Enemy Guide]] entry describing him as an assassin who became independent from the Bear Army.
*Counting the [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] Bears from [[Nyanko Defence Force]], Teacher Bear has had at least one variant for every trait.
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "Remember what Teacher Bear taught you!"

